{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node - <<'JS'\nconst fs=require('node:fs');const f=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('feedback.json'));f.testingFeedback=['Testing caught three game issues: an obsolete physics-module import, a clipped phone sector banner, and flagship camera/HUD framing. All were fixed. Test assertions also needed corrections for fuel-station overlap, floating-point gain precision, attract timing and the source-field count.','One was game breaking: the physics-module 404 prevented startup.','The full fixed-step browser playthrough proved both bridges, refueling, rolls, bursts, all three sectors and the flagship could reach victory. The official Hub harness was most helpful for multiplayer lifecycle checks.','WebGPU screenshots were least helpful because the headless WebGPU canvas was blank; state checks verified that backend and WebGL2 screenshots supplied the visual checks.'];f.engineFeedback[1]='I initially used an obsolete Rapier module filename; inspecting the installed 0.19.3 package fixed it. Screenshot review also exposed a camera/encounter framing mistake that simulation-only assertions missed.';fs.writeFileSync('feedback.json',JSON.stringify(f,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\ncommand -v biome\ncommand -v ruff\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node - <<'JS'\nconst fs=require('node:fs');const f=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('feedback.json'));f.testingFeedback=['Testing caught three game issues: an obsolete physics-module import, a clipped phone sector banner, and flagship camera/HUD framing. All were fixed. Test assertions also needed corrections for fuel-station overlap, floating-point gain precision, attract timing and the source-field count.','One was game breaking: the physics-module 404 prevented startup.','The full fixed-step browser playthrough proved both bridges, refueling, rolls, bursts, all three sectors and the flagship could reach victory. The official Hub harness was most helpful for multiplayer lifecycle checks.','WebGPU screenshots were least helpful because the headless WebGPU canvas was blank; state checks verified that backend and WebGL2 screenshots supplied the visual checks.'];f.engineFeedback[1]='I initially used an obsolete Rapier module filename; inspecting the installed 0.19.3 package fixed it. Screenshot review also exposed a camera/encounter framing mistake that simulation-only assertions missed.';fs.writeFileSync('feedback.json',JSON.stringify(f,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\ncommand -v biome\ncommand -v ruff\"","aggregated_output":"/home/micha/.local/bin/biome\n/home/micha/.local/bin/ruff\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
